flowchart TB
    accTitle: Recover a backup on a fresh installation
    accDescr: Both local vault files must be absent. Inspection authenticates the external backup and exposes counts only. A new Master Password, newly saved Recovery Key and replacement sign-in Authenticator are confirmed. Core rereads the backup at commit, creates a fresh DEK and config, validates staged wrappers and ciphertext, then begins a new unlocked login after successful persistence.
    start["First launch:\nRecover from encrypted backup"] --> empty{"Both .config and\n.storage absent?"}
    empty -->|No; including partial pair| blocked["Stop; preserve local files\nResolve existing storage first"]:::danger
    empty -->|Yes| inspect["Select backup + separate passphrase\nAuthenticate and validate full payload"]
    inspect -->|Wrong passphrase / invalid file| retry["Report failure\nNo vault created"]:::danger
    inspect -->|Valid| preview["Show format, date and item counts\nNo secrets in inspection result"]
    preview --> setup["Choose new Master Password\nSet up new sign-in Authenticator"]
    setup --> confirm["Verify current setup code\nSave and confirm new Recovery Key"]
    confirm -->|Cancel / invalid| retry
    confirm -->|Confirmed| revalidate["Core: recheck empty storage and inputs\nReread and authenticate backup"]
    revalidate --> create["KEY: generate fresh 256-bit DEK\nCreate two new config key slots"]:::key
    create --> encrypt["Re-encrypt entries under new DEK\nClear unknown group references"]
    encrypt --> commit[["Verify staged wrappers and ciphertext\nCommit new .config + .storage"]]
    commit -->|Failure| failed["Report persistence failure\nSee journal and rollback flow"]:::danger
    commit -->|Success| open["Start new unlocked login\nRecord backup verification time"]:::good
    classDef key fill:#ffffff,stroke:#2563eb,color:#0f172a,stroke-dasharray:4 3
    classDef danger fill:#fef2f2,stroke:#dc2626,color:#991b1b
    classDef good fill:#f0fdf4,stroke:#16a34a,color:#14532d
